<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib58.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arXiv preprint arXiv:2410.17268</em>, 2024.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib59" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhu et al. (2023)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Rui-Jie Zhu, Qihang Zhao, Guoqi Li, and Jason K Eshraghian.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Spikegpt: Generative pre-trained language model with spiking neural networks.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib59.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arXiv preprint arXiv:2302.13939</em>, 2023.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Mamba2 Block</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Mamba2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao &amp; Gu (2024)</a></cite> architecture consists of <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> stacked layers. At each layer, given the input <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> at time step <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the processing begins with a unified input projection:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}^{\prime}=\bm{u}_{t}\bm{W}_{\text{in}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(2H\cdot P+2N+H)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}^{\prime}=\bm{u}_{t}\bm{W}_{\text{in}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(2H\cdot P+2N+H)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x}_{t}^{\prime},\bm{B}_{t}^{\prime},\bm{C}_{t}^{\prime},{\Delta}_{t}^{\prime}=\text{Split}(\bm{u}_{t}^{\prime})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Split</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{z}_{t},\bm{x}_{t}^{\prime},\bm{B}_{t}^{\prime},\bm{C}_{t}^{\prime},{\Delta}_{t}^{\prime}=\text{Split}(\bm{u}_{t}^{\prime}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{\text{in}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times(2H\cdot P+2N+H)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{\text{in}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times(2H\cdot P+2N+H)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the input linear projection, <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is the model dimension, and <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H,P,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H,P,N</annotation></semantics></math> are the number of heads, dimension of each head and state dimension, respectively. The hyperparameter often keeps the relationship with <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\cdot P=2D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\cdot P=2D</annotation></semantics></math>. The projected features <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are then split across heads and along channels. We reshape the activation to obtain input <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}^{\prime(d)}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}^{\prime(d)}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}^{\prime(d)}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}^{\prime(d)}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for each head <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1,\dots,H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1,\dots,H</annotation></semantics></math>, The input-dependent variables for each head are computed as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{t}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{t}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp(-\Delta_{t}^{(d)}\exp(A^{(d)}))\in\mathbb{R}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp(-\Delta_{t}^{(d)}\exp(A^{(d)}))\in\mathbb{R},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{C}_{t}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{C}_{t}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(\text{Conv1d}(\bm{C}_{t}^{\prime}))\in\mathbb{R}^{N}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Conv1d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(\text{Conv1d}(\bm{C}_{t}^{\prime}))\in\mathbb{R}^{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{B}_{t}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{B}_{t}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(\text{Conv1d}(\bm{B}_{t}^{\prime}))\in\mathbb{R}^{N}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Conv1d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(\text{Conv1d}(\bm{B}_{t}^{\prime}))\in\mathbb{R}^{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{x}_{t}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{x}_{t}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(\text{Conv1d}(\bm{x}_{t}^{\prime(d)}))\in\mathbb{R}^{P}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Conv1d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(\text{Conv1d}(\bm{x}_{t}^{\prime(d)}))\in\mathbb{R}^{P},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}^{(d)}=\text{Softplus}(\Delta_{t}^{\prime(d)}+\Delta_{\text{bias}}^{(d)})\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Softplus</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>bias</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}^{(d)}=\text{Softplus}(\Delta_{t}^{\prime(d)}+\Delta_{\text{bias}}^{(d)})\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the SiLU activation and <span id="A1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Conv1d</span> denotes short causal convolution. The hidden state update and per-head output are computed as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{h}_{t}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{h}_{t}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{h}_{t-1}^{(d)}(\alpha_{t}^{(d)}I)+(\Delta_{t}^{(d)}\bm{B}_{t}^{(d)})\otimes\bm{x}_{t}^{(d)}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times P}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒉</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{h}_{t-1}^{(d)}(\alpha_{t}^{(d)}I)+(\Delta_{t}^{(d)}\bm{B}_{t}^{(d)})\otimes\bm{x}_{t}^{(d)}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times P},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{o}_{t}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒐</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{o}_{t}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{C}_{t}^{(d)}\bm{h}_{t}^{(d)}+\bm{D}^{(d)}\odot\bm{x}_{t}^{(d)}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑪</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{C}_{t}^{(d)}\bm{h}_{t}^{(d)}+\bm{D}^{(d)}\odot\bm{x}_{t}^{(d)}\in\mathbb{R}^{P},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Norm}\left(\text{Concat}(\bm{o}_{t}^{(1)},\dots,\bm{o}_{t}^{(H)})\odot z_{t}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{H\cdot P}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Norm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Concat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒐</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒐</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Norm}\left(\text{Concat}(\bm{o}_{t}^{(1)},\dots,\bm{o}_{t}^{(H)})\odot z_{t}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{H\cdot P},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{y}_{t}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{y}_{t}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{y}_{t}\bm{W}_{\text{out}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{y}_{t}\bm{W}_{\text{out}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the outer product, <math id="A1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}^{(d)}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}^{(d)}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(d)}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(d)}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are trainable parameters, <math id="A1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Norm}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Norm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Norm}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes RMS normalization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang &amp; Sennrich (2019)</a></cite>, and <math id="A1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{\text{out}}\in\mathbb{R}^{H\cdot P\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{\text{out}}\in\mathbb{R}^{H\cdot P\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> is the output projection matrix.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Activation Statistics</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To better understand the internal activation behavior of Mamba2, we visualize the distribution and structure of intermediate activations in Figures <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix B Activation Statistics ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Activation Statistics ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, and quantitatively evaluate their impact on model performance in Table <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix B Activation Statistics ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04595v1/u_distr_2d_ditribution.svg" id="A2.F3.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:648/377;" width="648" height="377"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F3.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="A2.F3.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒖</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.F3.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> distribution</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F3.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04595v1/y_distr_2d_ditribution.png" id="A2.F3.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:648/376;" width="648" height="376" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F3.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="A2.F3.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.F3.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> distribution</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="A2.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Activation distributions in Mamba2: (a) input projection <math id="A2.F3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Appendix A Mamba2 Block ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>),
(b) output projection <math id="A2.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq <a href="#A1.E21" title="In Appendix A Mamba2 Block ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04595v1/u_distr_index_layer.png" id="A2.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:648/229;" width="648" height="229" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="A2.F4.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒖</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.F4.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> statistics</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04595v1/y_distr_index_layer.png" id="A2.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:648/225;" width="648" height="225" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="A2.F4.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒚</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.F4.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> statistics</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A2.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Activation statistics across channels and tokens in Mamba2:
(a) input projection <math id="A2.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Appendix A Mamba2 Block ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>),
(b) output projection <math id="A2.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq <a href="#A1.E21" title="In Appendix A Mamba2 Block ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix B Activation Statistics ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> show the layer-wise distributions of <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> across the 24-layer Mamba2-130M model. While <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> values are relatively centered and stable across layers, <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> exhibits increasingly high-magnitude activation in deeper layers, with a wide dynamic range. Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Activation Statistics ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> further confirms this by visualizing the token-wise and channel-wise activation values, where <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> shows sparse but extreme peaks.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To simulate spike-based activations, we clamp the maximum activation value per channel to either 0 or 1, mimicking a spiking output. Table <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix B Activation Statistics ‣ SpikingMamba: Towards Energy-Efficient Large LanguageModels via Knowledge Distillation from Mamba" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows that this binarization leads to significant performance degradation across all tasks up to a 9.7% drop in average accuracy, demonstrating that high-magnitude activations play a critical role in preserving semantic fidelity. Notably, both <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> contribute to this effect, though the impact of clamping <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is more severe due to its broader variance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These results highlight a key challenge in deploying spike-based LLMs: naive binarization of positive activations leads to substantial loss in representational capacity, motivating our design of ternary neurons and auxiliary paths to preserve high-value semantics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 7</span>: </span><span id="A2.T7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Zero-shot accuracy obtained by setting the maximum activation in each channel to 1 or 0.</span></figcaption>
<div id="A2.T7.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:469.8pt;height:67.2pt;vertical-align:-31.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-20.7pt,3.0pt) scale(0.919101757789188,0.919101757789188) ;">
<table id="A2.T7.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T7.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
