<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 9</span>: </span><span id="A4.T9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The total energy consumption of the 1.3B model. The I-LIF is set as <math id="A4.T9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\times D=1\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\times D=1\times 4</annotation></semantics></math>, TI-LIF is set as <math id="A4.T9.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T\times D=1\times\pm 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo lspace="0em">±</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\times D=1\times\pm 4</annotation></semantics></math>. “SGC” means whether to use a smoothed gradient compensation path during training.</span></figcaption>
